  <h2>Where they overlap</h2>
  <p><code>stack exec --</code> forwards to <code>phantom exec --</code>. Stack does not itself expand placeholders or build a filled environment file. Qualify the installed execution and credential interface separately; this source does not establish equivalent behavior in another product.</p>
  <p>Storage, export, backup and runtime access have separate security boundaries. Verify the installed products and your configuration rather than inferring vendor access or encryption guarantees from this comparison.</p>

  <h2>Where Stack wins</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Provider-specific setup.</strong> <code>stack add stripe</code> accepts an existing Stripe credential and attempts Phantom storage and configuration writes. It does not create an account, and later failure can leave partial state.</li>
    <li><strong>Managed credential slots.</strong> Stack uses Phantom’s installed interface for credential persistence. Qualify its storage and runtime behavior; Stack source does not establish a universal encryption or vendor-access guarantee.</li>
    <li><strong>Explicit environment configuration.</strong> Stack can export a KEY= skeleton to <code>.env.example</code>. It does not generate a filled <code>.env.local</code>, resolve <code>phm_*</code> tokens or make project files safe to commit.</li>
    <li><strong>MCP control plane.</strong> Reviewed source declares 19 tools and conditional raw-file resources. The server forwards CLI output as text; inspect the installed client’s actual capabilities and project directory.</li>
    <li><strong>Source license.</strong> Stack source is MIT. This does not establish future service pricing or another vendor’s current terms.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where Doppler wins</h2>
  <p>Requirements to check against current Doppler documentation:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Team access requirements.</strong> Check current roles, permissions, environments and sharing behavior against your needs. This source comparison does not qualify those controls for either installed product.</li>
    <li><strong>Audit and compliance requirements.</strong> Verify current certifications, retention and access records directly with the vendor. A source roadmap is not an implemented audit guarantee.</li>
    <li><strong>Runtime integration requirements.</strong> Check SDK and process-execution contracts against your application. Stack’s <code>phantom exec</code> forwarding alone does not prove supported runtime secret delivery.</li>
    <li><strong>Existing workflows.</strong> Preserve a working setup while evaluating change. Provider setup with <code>stack add</code> does not automatically transfer secrets to another vault.</li>
    <li><strong>Support requirements.</strong> Check current support terms and installed-version behavior. Source {SOURCE_VERSION}, recorded public npm {PUBLISHED_VERSION} and native release binaries are distinct artifacts.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Can I use both?</h2>
  <p>If you keep an existing vault workflow, qualify any transfer separately. <code>stack add supabase</code> can create a project and persist credentials through Phantom, but this source does not implement a Doppler pipe or an automatic <code>phantom sync</code> bridge. Inspect partial state and permissions before attempting a migration.</p>

  <h2>Migration and caveats</h2>
  <p>This page describes reviewed source {SOURCE_VERSION}. Recorded public npm {PUBLISHED_VERSION} and native release binaries are separate artifacts. Team controls and runtime credential delivery require installed-product qualification. See <a href="/docs/phantom/">/docs/phantom</a>, <a href="/docs/mcp/">/docs/mcp</a> and <a href="/docs/providers/">/docs/providers</a> for the source-defined workflows.</p>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <h3>Is Stack a secret manager?</h3>
  <p>Stack coordinates supported provider setup and records configuration and credential slot names. Managed credentials use <a href="/docs/phantom/">Phantom</a>. Resource creation is adapter-specific and writes are sequential, not an atomic transaction. This source does not establish a native Doppler credential bridge.</p>

  <h3>Can I migrate from Doppler to Phantom?</h3>
  <p>A migration requires separately qualified export, import, backup and access-control procedures for the installed products. This Stack source does not establish a Doppler import or phantom sync command.</p>

  <h3>Which do YC startups use?</h3>
  <p>No startup adoption evidence is established here. Compare your team’s supported credential, provider setup and access-control requirements against current product documentation.</p>
</Docs>
